{{!-- POA Simple Variant — Straightforward durable power of attorney --}}
<h1 style="text-align:center; font-size:18pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">DURABLE POWER OF ATTORNEY</h1>
<p style="text-align:center; font-size:10pt; color:#555; margin-bottom:24pt;">
  State of New Jersey &mdash; Pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.1 <em>et seq.</em>
</p>

<p><strong>I, {{clientFullName}}</strong>, residing at {{personalInfo.address}}, {{personalInfo.city}}, {{personalInfo.county}} County, New Jersey {{personalInfo.zip}}, hereby appoint:</p>

<h2>ARTICLE I &mdash; APPOINTMENT OF AGENT</h2>

<p><strong>Primary Agent:</strong> {{fullName fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent}} 
{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.address}}, of {{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.address}}, {{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.city}}, {{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.state}} {{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.agent.zip}}{{/if}}</p>

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.alternateAgent}}
<p><strong>Alternate Agent:</strong> If my primary Agent is unable or unwilling to serve, I appoint {{fullName fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.alternateAgent}} as my alternate Agent.</p>
{{/if}}

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.successorAgent}}
<p><strong>Successor Agent:</strong> If both my primary and alternate Agents are unable or unwilling to serve, I appoint {{fullName fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.successorAgent}} as my successor Agent.</p>
{{/if}}

<h2>ARTICLE II &mdash; GRANT OF AUTHORITY</h2>

<p>I grant my Agent full power and authority to act on my behalf in all matters, including but not limited to the following, subject to any limitations stated herein:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Real property transactions</li>
  <li>Banking and financial transactions</li>
  <li>Business operations</li>
  <li>Insurance and annuity transactions</li>
  <li>Estate, trust, and beneficiary transactions</li>
  <li>Claims and litigation</li>
  <li>Tax matters</li>
  <li>Government benefits</li>
  <li>Retirement plan transactions</li>
  <li>Health care payment and insurance</li>
</ol>

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.giftingPower}}
<h2>ARTICLE III &mdash; GIFTING POWER</h2>
<p>My Agent is authorized to make gifts of my property, including gifts to the Agent, in amounts not exceeding the annual federal gift tax exclusion per donee per calendar year, consistent with my established gifting patterns, pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.13a.</p>
{{/if}}

<h2>ARTICLE {{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.giftingPower}}IV{{else}}III{{/if}} &mdash; DURABILITY</h2>

<p>This Power of Attorney is durable and shall not be affected by my subsequent disability or incapacity, pursuant to N.J.S.A. 46:2B-8.1. This Power of Attorney is effective <strong>{{#if (eq fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.effectiveDate 'immediate')}}immediately upon execution{{else}}upon my incapacity as determined by my attending physician{{/if}}</strong>.</p>

{{#if fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.limitations}}
<h2>LIMITATIONS</h2>
<p>{{fiduciaries.powerOfAttorney.limitations}}</p>
{{/if}}

<h2>GENERAL PROVISIONS</h2>

<p>a. My Agent shall not be held liable for any act done in good faith under this Power of Attorney.</p>
<p>b. Third parties may rely on the representations of my Agent as to all matters relating to any power granted herein.</p>
<p>c. This Power of Attorney revokes all prior powers of attorney previously executed by me.</p>
<p>d. If any provision of this Power of Attorney is held to be invalid, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect.</p>

<h2>EXECUTION</h2>

<p>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, I have executed this Durable Power of Attorney on this ______ day of ______________, 20___, at {{personalInfo.city}}, {{personalInfo.county}} County, New Jersey.</p>

